# Character reference photos

## Location
- George + family group shots: `lessons/assets/refs/george/` — tag index `lessons/assets/refs/george/CATALOG.md`
- Sylvia solo refs: `lessons/assets/refs/sylvia/` — tag index `lessons/assets/refs/sylvia/CATALOG.md`
- Mummy solo refs: `lessons/assets/refs/mummy/` — tag index `lessons/assets/refs/mummy/CATALOG.md`
- Daddy solo refs: `lessons/assets/refs/daddy/` — tag index `lessons/assets/refs/daddy/CATALOG.md`
- Photos in these folders are **tracked in git** (for shared agent / illustrator access)
- Put new photos **directly** into the matching folder and update that folder's `CATALOG.md` (do not use `ref/`)

## Cast ids (use these names in filenames and story art)
- `george` — boy ~5, lesson hero (short black hair with bangs, round face)
- `daddy` — father (~late 30s–40s; short dark hair, thin round metal glasses, chin mole) — solo refs: `lessons/assets/refs/daddy/`
- `mummy` — mother (~30s–40s; long dark hair, thin round metal glasses) — solo refs: `lessons/assets/refs/mummy/`
- `sylvia` — older sister (~12–14; long black hair, black rectangular glasses; often ponytail or cap outdoors) — solo refs: `lessons/assets/refs/sylvia/`

## Filename pattern
`{subjects}-{setting}-{pose-or-mood}[-variant].jpg`  
Example: `george-daddy-outdoors-lifevest-smile.jpg` (George listed first)

## When generating lesson illustrations
1. Read `docs/family-refs.md` (one-page map), `docs/cast-bible.md`, and `.cursor/skills/picture-book-consistency/SKILL.md` **before** drawing
2. Open the matching `CATALOG.md`, then **Read** the chosen photo(s) and the bible’s lock frames
3. Default George likeness: `george-solo-bed-smile.jpg` (`priority: primary`); strong face/cover ref: `george-solo-sofa-alphabet-smile.jpg`
4. **Family faces (required — Lesson 7 ran generic when agents used only the Halloween group shot):**
   - Sylvia: `sylvia-solo-outdoors-graduation-smile.jpg` (`priority: primary`)
   - Mummy: `mummy-solo-indoor-smile.png` (`priority: primary`)
   - Daddy: `daddy-solo-indoor-vehicle-neutral.png` (solo) or `george-daddy-outdoors-pavilion-neutral.jpg` (with George)
5. Group shots (`george-daddy-mummy-sylvia-*`, Halloween family) are for **who / height / pose** only — not the only face lock
6. Dragons: Pip waist-to-chest vs George; Ember knee-high and smaller than Pip. Do not invent a new dragon body each page
7. Match cast + mood tags from the catalog to the story beat
8. Keep George, Daddy, Sylvia, and Mummy consistent across the whole lesson; do not invent a different face per page
9. Never embed these private photos in published HTML; only AI/drawn picture-book art goes under `lessons/assets/lesson-XX/`
10. Lesson 7 home clothes: draw Daddy／Mummy／Sylvia from `lessons/assets/refs/cast/wild-things-family-sheet.png` (pajamas, socks or barefoot). `wild-things-sheet.png` is George + beasts only — it does not lock family outfits

## AI voice (paired with likeness)
- Fixed voice per cast id: see `scripts/voices.json` and `docs/character-voices.md`
- George → `george`, Daddy → `daddy`; dragons Pip / Ember → `pip` / `ember`
